@startuml
title StockPilot - Sequence Diagram: Investor

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

actor Investor
participant "React UI" as UI
participant "API Client\n(axios)" as API
participant "FastAPI\nRouter" as Router
participant "Auth\n(JWT / RBAC)" as Auth
participant "Analysis\nService" as Analysis
participant "StockPredictor\n(XGBoost)" as Model
participant "FinBERT" as FinBERT
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Yahoo Finance" as YF

== 1. Authentication ==

Investor -> UI : enter email + password
UI -> API : POST /auth/login
API -> Router : HTTP request
Router -> DB : SELECT user WHERE email = ?
DB --> Router : user record
alt invalid credentials
    Router --> API : 401 Invalid email or password
else valid
    Router -> Router : verify bcrypt hash
    Router -> Router : issue access + refresh JWT
    Router --> API : 200 {tokens, user}
end
API -> UI : store tokens in localStorage
UI --> Investor : redirect to Investor Dashboard

== 2. Explainable AI verdict (six-factor) ==

Investor -> UI : select ticker, adjust six weight sliders
UI -> API : GET /analysis/{ticker}/factors?w_*
API -> Router : request + Bearer token
Router -> Auth : authenticate
Auth -> DB : SELECT user WHERE id = sub
Auth --> Router : authenticated user
Router -> Analysis : compute factor scores

Analysis -> YF : fetch 6 months OHLCV
YF --> Analysis : price data
Analysis -> Analysis : calculate 23 technical indicators
Analysis -> FinBERT : analyse recent headlines
FinBERT -> YF : fetch news headlines
YF --> FinBERT : headlines
FinBERT --> Analysis : sentiment score 0-100

alt no headlines available
    Analysis -> Analysis : fall back to OBV trend proxy
end

Analysis -> Analysis : score 6 factors, apply weights
Analysis -> Analysis : composite -> BUY / HOLD / SELL + confidence
Analysis --> Router : verdict + per-factor breakdown
Router --> API : 200 factors response
API --> UI : render verdict card and factor bars
UI --> Investor : explainable recommendation

== 3. Live model prediction (XGBoost) ==

UI -> API : GET /predictions/{ticker}/live
API -> Router : request
Router -> Model : predict(ticker)
opt model not loaded
    Model -> Model : load model.pkl (once per process)
end
Model -> YF : fetch 6 months OHLCV
YF --> Model : price data
Model -> Model : build features, predict_proba()
Model -> Model : map probability to BUY / HOLD / SELL
Model --> Router : signal, confidence, probabilities
Router -> DB : INSERT INTO predictions
DB --> Router : persisted row
Router --> API : 200 prediction
API --> UI : show verdict + MODEL LIVE badge

== 4. Backtest a strategy ==

Investor -> UI : choose period, click Run Backtest
UI -> API : GET /analysis/{ticker}/backtest
API -> Router : request
Router -> Analysis : run simulation
Analysis -> YF : fetch historical OHLCV
YF --> Analysis : price data

alt fewer than 60 rows
    Analysis --> Router : 400 Insufficient data
else sufficient data
    Analysis -> Analysis : composite score for every day
    Analysis -> Analysis : derive entry / exit signals
    Analysis -> Analysis : simulate portfolio (vectorbt)\nfees 0.1%, slippage 0.05%, trailing stop
    Analysis --> Router : metrics + equity curve + trade ledger
end
Router --> API : 200 backtest result
API --> UI : render statistics and chart
Investor -> UI : Download log
UI --> Investor : CSV of every trade (generated in browser)

== 5. Manage portfolio ==

Investor -> UI : add holding (ticker, quantity, cost)
UI -> API : POST /portfolio
API -> Router : request
Router -> Auth : authenticate
Router -> YF : look up current price
YF --> Router : live price
Router -> DB : INSERT INTO holdings
DB --> Router : created holding
Router --> API : 201 Created
API --> UI : refresh list
UI --> Investor : updated valuation and profit / loss

note over Investor, DB
  An investor cannot publish a strategy.
  POST /strategies/{id}/publish is rejected
  with 403 by require_role(analyst, admin).
end note

@enduml
